Fixed. All bugs were in `ini/ini.go` (`Parse`); tests were untouched. Changes:

1. **Trim lines first** (ini.go:58) — indented section lines, keys, and comments were mis-parsed before
2. **`#` comment lines** (ini.go:59) — only `;` was handled, so `# another comment` was a syntax error
3. **Lower-case section names** (ini.go:63) — `[Server]` was stored as-is but `Get` looks up lower-cased
4. **First `=` splits key/value** (ini.go:66) — was `LastIndex`, so `url = http://x/?a=b` corrupted the key
5. **Inline comments only at ` ;`/` #`** (ini.go:74,87) — was any `;`; now `1;2` and `hash#tag` stay intact, and quoted values (`"x ; y # z"`) are protected by checking quotes first
6. **Quoted values keep inner whitespace** (ini.go:73) — removed the inner `TrimSpace` so `"  /srv  "` → `  /srv  `
7. **Repeated keys overwrite** (ini.go:80) — was keep-first

Also applied gofmt to a pre-existing one-liner. Verified: `go test -count=1 ./...` exits 0, `go vet` clean, plus a scratch program confirming all documented behaviors the tests don't cover (overwrite, `#` comments, tab before `;`, quoted preservation, first-`=` split, syntax error line numbers).
